{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"puppylike-emo-rasbora","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nGerrit Verify remains variable and macOS is usually the completion critical path, while Ubuntu cells consume contentious runner capacity. Existing duration logs identify individual tests and fixtures over one second, but there is no current exhaustive audit mapping every such cost to its unique reachable failure mode, faster overlapping coverage, prior ticket decisions, and safe remediation options. This is analysis only: preserve real E2E/integration seams and do not infer that a slow test is redundant from duration alone.\n\n## Plan\n- Build a normalized inventory of every pytest setup/call/teardown phase over 1.0s from recent representative successful Gerrit Verify logs, retaining run id, OS/Python cell, phase, and duration; use local timing only to resolve attribution gaps.\n- Group parameterized nodes and coherent fixture families, inspect their production/test paths, and identify the unique failure mode or contract each reaches plus any faster overlapping tests.\n- For each possible removal, refactor, sample, static corpus, fixture-scope, or tier move, search ticket titles/descriptions/comments/history for prior bugs, rejected approaches, blind spots, and accepted precedents.\n- Compare safe proposals with popular actively maintained OSS practice where it materially informs fidelity.\n- Quantify expected per-cell wall and aggregate runner savings, distinguishing macOS critical-path impact from Ubuntu contention and labeling xdist/host-variance uncertainty.\n- Produce evidence-backed keep/refactor/move recommendations and ranked next actions without changing code, tests, workflows, or CI.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Inventory covers every observed pytest phase over 1.0s in the selected representative runs and records duration, platform/cell, phase, and run id.\n- [ ] Every inventoried node or coherent family has a keep/refactor/move recommendation and a cited unique failure-mode or coverage rationale.\n- [ ] Every optimization proposal cites relevant tracker history, including status and any prior rejection or gotcha.\n- [ ] Proposals preserve real external, process, filesystem, concurrency, packaging, and platform seams when mocks cannot provide equivalent confidence.\n- [ ] Expected macOS wall-clock and aggregate Ubuntu/total runner savings are quantified without treating summed xdist test-seconds as additive wall time.\n- [ ] Measurement gaps and confidence are explicit.\n- [ ] Ranked next actions are recorded on this ticket; no implementation or CI dispatch is performed.","id":"815d-8f56-7237-4b58","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["audit","ci","test-runtime"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Audit every CI test over one second for unique confidence and removable cost"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786816614312327001,"uuid":"fb89fa0b-dd52-41a7-a803-650888bbe1cb"}